q:
What is printed?

class A:
    def f(self): return "A"
class B(A):
    def f(self): return "B" + super().f()
class C(A):
    def f(self): return "C" + super().f()
class D(B, C):
    def f(self): return "D" + super().f()
print(D().f())

A) DBCA
B) DBCA with an extra A
C) DABC
D) D followed by B only

How many distinct calls to fib are actually executed (including the initial one) when fib(10) is called for the first time on a fresh cache?

import functools
@functools.lru_cache(maxsize=None)
def fib(n):
    return n if n < 2 else fib(n-1) + fib(n-2)

A) 10
B) 11
C) 177
D) 89
